%% Diagram: Snowflake warehouse scaling — scale-up vs scale-out
%% Source lecture: Snowflake Complete Masterclass - Section 7 (Performance)
%% Description:  Scale-up (single, bigger) vs scale-out (more clusters of the
%%               same size).  Scale-up = each query uses more CPUs/RAM.
%%               Scale-out = more concurrent queries, same per-query size.
%% Author: Prem Vishnoi <pvishnoi@avilx.com>
```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph UP["Scale UP  (ALTER WAREHOUSE SET WAREHOUSE_SIZE)"]
        XS["1 × X-Small<br/>(1 server)"] --> M["1 × Medium<br/>(1 server, 4× bigger)"]
    end

    subgraph OUT["Scale OUT  (MAX_CLUSTER_COUNT > 1)"]
        XS2["2 × X-Small<br/>(2 servers)"] -. "concurrent queries" .-> XS3["2 × X-Small<br/>(2 servers)"]
    end

    Q1["Query A"] --> XS
    Q1B["Query A (bigger)"] --> M
    QA["Query A"] --> XS2
    QB["Query B (concurrent)"] --> XS3

    style UP  fill:#FEF3C7,stroke:#B45309
    style OUT fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#166534
```
